  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The country programme outcome aims at improving the government&#x2019;s capacities for report writing and the creation and increase of the capacity of governments in the Arab region to participate and contribute in a proactive and meaningful manner in the reporting processes under the ILO Constitution that relate to ILS. Against the background that the quality and relevance of ILO reports and surveys depend on the quality and type of information the governments provide with their reports, the focus of this programme is to provide the necessary tools and techniques to government officials involved in the preparation of the government&#x2019;s reports that feed into the drafting of the upcoming General Surveys (R205 and C 158). In addition, the programme aims to clarify the roles of the social partners involved in the preparation of the government&#x2019;s report as well as the sequence and timeline to be followed for preparing the reports</narrative>
  </description>
